---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

const updated = '22 August 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} handles data: tool input never leaves your browser, and what the analytics and advertising do collect.`}
  canonicalPath="/privacy-policy/"
>
  <div class="container page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="eyebrow">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        Anything you type or paste into a tool on this site stays in your browser. It is
        never transmitted to us or to anyone else, and we could not read it if we wanted
        to. Separately, like most websites, we collect basic anonymous traffic statistics
        and show advertising — both are described in full below.
      </p>

      <h2>Data you enter into tools</h2>
      <p>
        Every tool on this site runs as JavaScript inside your own browser. There is no
        server-side processing, no database, and no logging of tool input. When you paste
        JSON, a token, a password to hash, or any other content into a tool:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>It is processed locally by your browser and then discarded when you close or reload the page.</li>
        <li>It is never sent over the network to this site or any third party.</li>
        <li>It is never stored, logged, or retained in any form.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You can verify this independently by opening your browser's developer tools, going
        to the Network tab, and using any tool on the site.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to understand which pages are used and how quickly
        they load. It is cookieless and does not fingerprint or track individuals across
        sites. It records aggregate information such as page URL, referring site, country,
        browser type, and page-load timings. It does not record anything you type.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        This site is funded by display advertising served by Google AdSense. Third-party
        vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to
        this and other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its
        partners to serve ads based on your visit to this and other sites.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can opt out of personalised advertising by visiting
        <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="nofollow noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>,
        or opt out of third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalised advertising at
        <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="nofollow noopener">aboutads.info</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom or Switzerland, you
        will be asked for consent before any personalised advertising cookies are set, and
        you can change or withdraw that consent at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Local storage</h2>
      <p>
        The site stores a single value in your browser's local storage: your light or dark
        theme preference. It never leaves your device and is not used to identify you. If
        you have not chosen a theme, nothing is stored at all.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Because we do not collect personal data through the tools, there is generally no
        personal data of yours for us to access, correct, or delete. For the advertising
        cookies described above, your choices are managed through the consent controls and
        the opt-out links in that section.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes materially, the "last updated" date above will change. The
        commitment that tool input never leaves your browser is architectural — the site
        has no server capable of receiving it — and is not something we intend to alter.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-block: var(--space-6) var(--space-7);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
</style>
